# SonoJS direction (RTL + LTR)

Every new component, block, chart, and docs chrome piece MUST support both writing directions from day one. Direction is a **core system concern**, not a per-component afterthought.

## Inheritance

- Writing direction **inherits** from the nearest ancestor `dir` (normally `<html dir="…">`).
- **Do not** hardcode `dir="ltr"` or `dir="rtl"` on components/layouts unless creating an intentional isolated island (e.g. a code sample that must stay LTR).
- To force a subtree direction in demos, wrap with `DirectionProvider` from `@/components/direction`.
- Read direction with `useDirection()` from `@/hooks/use-direction` or `@/components/direction`.

## Layout & spacing (required)

Use **logical** Tailwind / CSS only:

| Avoid (physical) | Use (logical) |
|------------------|---------------|
| `ml-*` `mr-*` | `ms-*` `me-*` |
| `pl-*` `pr-*` | `ps-*` `pe-*` |
| `left-*` `right-*` | `start-*` `end-*` |
| `text-left` `text-right` | `text-start` `text-end` |
| `border-l` `border-r` | `border-s` `border-e` |
| `rounded-l-*` `rounded-r-*` | `rounded-s-*` `rounded-e-*` |
| `scroll-ml` / physical popover align hacks | logical alignment / `getStartSide(dir)` |

## Icons & motion

- Directional icons (chevron, arrow, caret along inline axis): add class `icon-dir` (see `styles/direction.css`) or `rtl:rotate-180` / `[dir=rtl]:scale-x-[-1]`.
- Do **not** mirror logos, brand marks, or bidirectional-neutral icons.
- Sheet/drawer edges: use `getStartSide(dir)` / `getEndSide(dir)` from `@/lib/direction` — never hardcode only `left` or only `right` for start-edge chrome.

## Interaction

- Focus rings, hit targets, and menus must remain usable in both directions.
- Popovers/dropdowns: prefer `align="start"` / `align="end"` over physical assumptions.
- Animations that slide along the inline axis must reverse in RTL (or use logical transforms).

## Registry checklist (new UI / block / chart)

Before merging a new registry item:

1. No physical `ml`/`mr`/`pl`/`pr`/`left`/`right`/`text-left`/`text-right` for layout.
2. No hardcoded `dir="ltr"` on the component root.
3. Directional icons marked with `icon-dir` when needed.
4. Preview works under both `<DirectionProvider dir="ltr">` and `dir="rtl"`.
5. Documented in the component docs with an LTR/RTL preview when the control has inline asymmetry.

## Docs site chrome

Site default may be `dir="ltr"` on `<html>`. Section layouts must **inherit**, not re-assert direction, so wrapping demos in `DirectionProvider` works.
